[size=5][b]PalModManager (PMM) - Next-Gen Mod Manager & Config Editor for Palworld[/b][/size]

[line]
Latest version: 1.4.0

Changelog: You can find the latest update notes in the pinned comments section or check the full history on [url=https://github.com/olivo28/PalModManager]GitHub[/url].

[line]

[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[b]PalModManager[/b] is a modern, high-performance desktop application built specifically for [b]Palworld[/b] players and modders on [b]Steam[/b] and [b]Xbox Game Pass (PC)[/b].

Unlike generic mod managers, PalModManager is tailor-made for Palworld: it natively handles all mod structures ([b]UE4SS[/b], [b]PalSchema[/b], [b]Pak[/b], [b]LogicMods[/b], and [b]Hybrids[/b]), provides conflict detection, and includes a full-featured built-in JSON configuration code editor.

Built with [b]Tauri v2[/b] and [b]Rust[/b], PalModManager launches instantly and uses minimal RAM and CPU.

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download [b]PalModManager[/b] from the Files section.[/*]
[*]Run [b]PalModManager.exe[/b] (or use the portable standalone exe directly without installation).[/*]
[*]Open [b]Settings[/b] (⚙ icon) and select your Palworld installation directory.[/*]
[*]Drag & drop any mod [i].zip[/i], [i].rar[/i], or [i].7z[/i] file directly into the app window to install![/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Ultra-Fast & Lightweight[/b]: Built on Rust and Tauri v2 for instantaneous response times and zero bloat.[/*]
[*][b]Smart Mod Auto-Detection[/b]: Automatically identifies and categorizes UE4SS, PalSchema, Pak, LogicMods, and Hybrids.[/*]
[*][b]Interactive ZIP File Tree Preview (New!)[/b]: Open a collapsible tree previewer in both single and batch mod installers to inspect ZIP contents and projected targets in real-time before installing.[/*]
[*][b]Dynamic UE4SS Load Order Manager (New!)[/b]: Manage loading sequences interactively with a drag-and-drop ordering interface in the sidebar, syncing state transitions between `enabled.txt` and `mods.txt` dynamically.[/*]
[*][b]Integrated Mod Packer & Manifesting (New!)[/b]: Package mods with custom target routing, author/version tags, and Nexus IDs. Saves layout manifests into a dedicated `modinfo.pmm.json` file inside the ZIP, enabling instant, heuristic-free native installation on client machines.[/*]
[*][b]Pre-installed Mod Scanner (New!)[/b]: Scans local game directories and parses `modinfo.pmm.json` to load rich mod descriptions, versions, and authors automatically.[/*]
[*][b]Mod Conflict & Compatibility Scanner[/b]: Analyzes enabled mods to identify table row overlaps (PalSchema overrides) and hook overlaps (multiple mods hooking the same engine function in Lua) in a side-by-side split view.[/*]
[*][b]Lua Hotkeys Manager[/b]: Scan active Lua scripts for keybind configurations (`RegisterKeyBind`), display them in an interactive table, highlight conflicts, and inline edit the key combinations.[/*]
[*][b]Smart Heuristic ZIP Unpacker[/b]: Never worry about how mod files are structured. Generic managers fail when mod authors zip their files with custom structures or nested folders. PalModManager implements a custom layout sanitizer that automatically parses, flattens, and reorganizes any zipped layout into clean game-ready directories before installation, bypassing platform wrappers like `(STEAM)` and `(XBOX)` seamlessly.[/*]
[*][b]Automated Dependency Management[/b]: Detects missing core dependencies (UE4SS or PalSchema) and offers one-click automatic installation using official GitHub releases.[/*]
[*][b]Batch & Drag-and-Drop Installation[/b]: Drop single or multiple zip files to preview mod details, check versions, and install in bulk.[/*]
[*][b]Installed Version Warnings[/b]: The upgrade assistant explicitly warns and displays your currently installed version when dragging files to update existing mods.[/*]
[*][b]Mod Library[/b]: Maintain a centralized library of downloaded mods complete with auto-fetched NexusMods thumbnails, authors, and summary metadata.[/*]
[*][b]Reactive Profile Manager (File Explorer style)[/b]: Create and switch between isolated mod profiles (e.g. Singleplayer, Multiplayer, Hardcore) with instant physical folder deployment. Shows virtual folders as folder cards side-by-side with ungrouped mods, supporting double-click navigation and a right-click custom folder options menu.[/*]
[*][b]ID Stability System[/b]: Uses the [b]Nexus Mod ID[/b] or [b]Sanitized descriptive names[/b] to identify mods (no random UUIDs), ensuring upgrades and profile matching are 100% stable.[/*]
[*][b]Built-in Code Editor[/b]: Edit mod json and jsonc configuration files directly within the application with syntax highlighting, auto-formatting, search (Ctrl+F), and safety checks preventing loss of changes when switching profiles.[/*]
[*][b]NexusMods Metadata & Update Sync[/b]: Automatically check for mod updates and sync metadata/thumbnails directly from NexusMods. Includes "Open Updates" to open all Nexus pages for mods with available updates at once.[/*]
[*][b]Settings & Database Inspector[/b]: Advanced database inspector to view and edit Mods, Profiles, and Settings tables with raw JSON record validation, custom app storage redirection/migration, and toolbar UI scaling (80% to 180%).[/*]
[*][b]Modern Dark Mode[/b]: Sleek glassmorphism UI designed for maximum usability and aesthetic clarity.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]🐧 Linux Native Support & Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
PalModManager features native compatibility for Linux systems. If you run the Linux version and experience crashes on startup or a blank screen, execute the app using these parameters:
[list]
[*] [b]Force X11 Backend[/b] (resolves crashes related to Wayland windowing layers in WebKitGTK):
[code]GDK_BACKEND=x11 ./palmodmanager[/code][/*]
[*] [b]Disable DMABUF Rendering[/b] (resolves blank/invisible interface issues caused by graphics driver/Nvidia rendering conflicts):
[code]WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1 ./palmodmanager[/code][/*]
[*] [b]Combined execution[/b]:
[code]GDK_BACKEND=x11 WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1 ./palmodmanager[/code][/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]⚠️ Important Safety & Backup Recommendation[/b][/size]
[quote]
[b]Before using PalModManager (or installing mods in general), we strongly recommend manually backing up your game's mod directories.[/b][/quote]
While [b]PalModManager automatically handles and backs up UE4SS/PalSchema/Paks files[/b], it is always best practice to create a copy of the following folders in your Palworld directory:
[list]
[*]📁 [i]Pal/Content/Paks[/i][/*]
[*]📁 [i]Pal/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss[/i] (Steam) or [i]Pal/Binaries/WinGDK/ue4ss[/i] (Xbox GDK)[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]🛡️ Anti-Virus & False Positives Note[/b][/size]
This application is built using [b]Rust + Tauri[/b] for maximum efficiency and security.

Because this is an independent community project without a commercial Code Signing Certificate, some antivirus engines (like Windows Defender or SecureAge) may trigger a [b]false positive[/b] (e.g., [i]Trojan:Win32/Wacatac.B!ml[/i] or similar flags).
[list]
[*][b]Why this happens[/b]: Heuristic AI and machine learning analysis ([i]!ml[/i]) frequently flags unsigned executables that perform folder and file system modifications (such as injecting or switching files in your Steam Palworld directories).[/*]
[*][b]Is it safe?[/b]: Absolutely. The program is completely clean. If you download it from the official page, there is no threat. [/*]
[*][b]Workaround[/b]: If Windows Defender blocks the manager, click [i]"More Info"[/i] -> [i]"Run Anyway"[/i] on the SmartScreen prompt, or add [i]palmodmanager.exe[/i] to your antivirus exclusions list.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Game[/b]: Palworld (Steam or PC Game Pass).[/*]
[*][b]OS[/b]: Windows 10 / Windows 11 (64-bit) or Linux (Ubuntu, Debian, SteamOS, etc.).[/*]
[*][b]Optional Dependencies[/b]:
  - UE4SS (PalModManager can install this for you automatically).
  - PalSchema (PalModManager can install this for you automatically).[/*]
[/list]

